1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,780
Here is the Hauser Mark Four—four core bays, each with an expandable theater display.

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:11,140
Top bay: the Wideband Tuner scans six wavebands, four frequency maps, and expands full screen.

3
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:17,740
Left bay: the Correlator decodes live cameras, phase plots, and cipher cartridges, then pops open.

4
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:24,180
Center bay: Galactic Astrometry slews our phased-array beam, grades SINPO merit, and opens the Atlas.

5
00:00:24,180 --> 00:00:30,220
Right bay: the Verification Deck decodes slow-scan QSL cards and expands the hardware dossier.

6
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:36,020
Now let's operate the Tuner, jumping across ninety-meter cryo-scatter, octal relays, and hydrogen masers.

7
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:41,600
Spinning the vernier wheel slides the illuminated callsign scale and narrows the crystal passband filter.

8
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:48,270
Next door, the frequency map cycles between spectrogram waterfall, band allocation, three-D ridges, and Doppler phase.

9
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:55,390
Expanding the Band-Plan Scanner displays all six wavebands alongside intermediate-frequency passband zoom and Doppler lock.

10
00:00:55,390 --> 00:01:01,560
In the Correlator Bay on Callisto, we lock live arc-camera video and expand the Visual Theater.

11
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:07,780
Tuning the Triangulum beacon in Three-D Spectrum mode pairs the hydrogen maser spike with a Lissajous rose.

12
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:14,580
On Trojan Octal frames, Algorithm One faults, while Algorithm Two locks and translates the Euclidean telemetry.

13
00:01:14,580 --> 00:01:20,280
We pop open the full Cipher Theater, then audition the voice intercept and interval signal on the scope.

14
00:01:20,280 --> 00:01:26,800
In the Center Bay, tuning slews our phased-array beam while the twenty-segment S-meter and SINPO matrix lock.

15
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:34,520
Expanding the Galactic Atlas reveals our Ceres Foundry parallax triangle, pulsar clock, and spiral-arm relay hops.

16
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:41,560
In the Right Bay, triggering a Robot-Twenty-Four slow-scan burst wipes down line by line to decode the QSL card.

17
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:48,780
Expanding the QSL Dossier reveals the subcarrier clue, while the memory tabs below cycle verified operator logs.

18
00:01:48,780 --> 00:01:54,880
In summary: the Mark Four pairs a six-band tuner and four-mode spectrum map with an expandable correlator.

19
00:01:54,880 --> 00:02:02,440
And it unites galactic beam triangulation and SINPO grading with slow-scan e-QSL dossiers and full-screen modals.

20
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:11,090
Four bays, four expandable theaters, one complete deep-space DX workstation—seventy-three from Galactic Outpost Radio Nine.
